        "The IL-10 result is limited to the tested culture conditions and time points.",
        "These measurements do not establish that all inflammatory or pathway outputs are uniform or divergent across cell types."
      ],
      "rationale": "Observation o04 explicitly reports TNF-alpha increases in both cell types but different IL-10 responses. Observation o05 reports STING-pathway findings in both cell types, so the cytokine divergence should refine rather than replace the broader prolonged-DAMP claim."
    },
    {
      "target_ids": ["n04"],
      "evidence_ids": ["o06"],
      "availability": "relevant_visible",
      "assessment": "Under 48-hour DAMP exposure, H-151 reversed the TNF-alpha increase and restored phagocytic readouts in both cell types; IL-10 appeared unaffected by H-151. This supports a shared inhibitor-sensitive TNF-alpha result in the tested cultures, but does not erase the distinct untreated IL-10 responses.",
