      "assessment": "The reported panel results show higher fracture strain than untreated pristine CFRP (5.62%) for the described high-temperature-treated uncoated group (13.2%), LD-coated fabric treated at 700 °C (16.96%), LD at 900 °C (8.94%), and HD at 700 °C (22.0%). HD at 700 °C is the highest reported value among these groups. The uncoated group's treatment temperature and heating mode are not specified in its reporting sentence, and the HD observation does not specify heating mode.",
