      "limitations": [
        "The number of specimens and variability or statistical uncertainty are not reported for these tensile results in the supplied observations.",
        "The condition of the high-temperature-treated uncoated group in o34 is not identified as 700 °C or 900 °C, and its heating mode is unstated.",
        "The heating mode for the HD 700 °C group is unstated; the packet indicates LH was only applied to 700 °C but does not establish the mode for each tensile group.",
        "The observations report outcomes, not evidence that a particular interfacial or deformation mechanism caused the strain changes."
      ],
      "rationale": "Observations o33–o37 explicitly report fracture-strain measurements relevant to n02. They support describing the measured outcomes and their stated comparisons, but do not establish statistical reliability or isolate the effects of coating and heating in comparisons that vary both."
    },
    {
      "target_ids": ["n03"],
      "evidence_ids": ["o33", "o34", "o35", "o36", "o37"],
      "availability": "relevant_visible",
      "assessment": "Untreated pristine CFRP had a reported strength of 514 MPa. The high-temperature-treated uncoated group was reported at 389 MPa; LD-coated CFRP was 298 MPa at 700 °C and 244 MPa at 900 °C; HD-coated CFRP was 331 MPa at 700 °C and was reported to retain more strength than the LD counterpart. These are reported group outcomes, not estimates with supplied uncertainty.",
      "scope": "Reported maximum tensile strength in cured CFRP panels for the groups and treatment conditions stated in observations o33–o37.",
      "limitations": [
        "The number of specimens and variability or statistical uncertainty are not reported for these tensile results in the supplied observations.",
        "The condition of the high-temperature-treated uncoated group in o34 is not identified as 700 °C or 900 °C, and its heating mode is unstated.",
        "The heating mode for the HD 700 °C group is unstated.",
        "Strength differences between pristine and treated/coated groups cannot be attributed to coating alone because coating and heat treatment vary together in those comparisons.",
        "The tensile observations alone do not establish the causal mechanism for strength loss or retention."
      ],
      "rationale": "Observations o33–o37 directly report tensile-strength values and, for HD versus LD at 700 °C, explicitly report higher strength retention for HD. The scope and missing uncertainty information limit stronger generalizations."
