      "kind": "reported_tensile_pattern",
      "target_ids": ["n02", "n03"],
      "description": "At 700 °C, the reported HD group had greater fracture strain and strength than the LD group (22.0% and 331 MPa versus 16.96% and 298 MPa), while both had lower reported strength than untreated pristine CFRP (514 MPa). The HD–LD comparison is reported at the same treatment temperature, but its heating mode is unstated.",
      "basis_ids": ["o33", "o35", "o37"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "comparison_scope_limitation",
      "target_ids": ["n02", "n03"],
      "description": "The 13.2% strain and 389 MPa strength for high-temperature-treated uncoated CFRP are relevant observations, but the reporting sentence does not identify the treatment temperature or heating mode. Comparisons of that group with untreated pristine CFRP therefore cannot be assigned to a specific thermal condition from this packet.",
      "basis_ids": ["o33", "o34"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "mechanistic_support_limitation",
      "target_ids": ["n02", "n03"],
      "description": "The tensile observations support the reported property outcomes, but by themselves do not establish the causal explanations in existing interpretation i06 for strength reduction or strain increase.",
      "basis_ids": ["o35", "o37"]
    }
  ],
  "proposed_updates": [
    {
      "operation": "ADD_ASPECT",
      "target_ids": ["n02", "n03"],
      "basis_ids": ["o37"],
      "rationale": "The existing map records the LD 700 °C tensile result in n16 but has no corresponding claim node for the directly reported HD 700 °C result. Add a narrowly scoped claim capturing the HD observation without changing n16 or implying that the heating mode is known.",
      "content": {
        "add_nodes": [
          {
            "id": "n17",
            "type": "claim",
            "statement": "At 700 °C, CFRP from HD Ni-coated fabric showed an extensive plastic plateau, a maximum fracture strain of 22.0% (291.46% above pristine CFRP) and a maximum tensile strength of 331 MPa; its reported strength retention was higher than that of the LD counterpart.",
            "source_spans": ["sp_f06bd3cf2b664f68"]
          }
        ],
        "add_edges": [
          {
            "id": "edge_tens_hd_ductility",
            "type": "refinement",
            "source_id": "n02",
            "target_id": "n17",
            "source_spans": ["sp_f06bd3cf2b664f68"]
          },
          {
            "id": "edge_tens_hd_strength",
            "type": "refinement",
            "source_id": "n03",
            "target_id": "n17",
            "source_spans": ["sp_f06bd3cf2b664f68"]
          }
        ],
        "replace_nodes": [],
        "replace_edges": [],
        "remove_edge_ids": []
      }
    }
  ],
  "verification_needs": [
    {
      "target_ids": ["n02", "n03"],
      "unresolved_question": "How reproducible are the reported tensile differences, and what exact thermal conditions apply to the incompletely specified comparison groups?",
      "needed_observations": [
        "Specimen counts and replicate-level or summarized variability for tensile strength and fracture strain in each group.",
        "The exact treatment temperature and heating mode for the high-temperature-treated uncoated group in o34.",
        "The heating mode used for the HD 700 °C tensile group.",
        "Statistical comparisons, if performed, for the stated between-group differences."
      ],
      "comparison_or_control": "Compare pristine untreated CFRP, uncoated heat-treated CFRP, LD and HD CFRP at matched thermal conditions, with epoxy system and cure held fixed.",
      "why_informative": "These observations would clarify uncertainty in the reported group differences and distinguish coating-related contrasts from differences due to thermal treatment, while supporting an assessment of reproducibility.",
      "missing_design_information": [
        "Tensile specimen counts and variability are not supplied for the reported groups.",
        "The treatment temperature and heating mode for the uncoated high-temperature group are not specified in o34.",
        "The heating mode for the HD 700 °C tensile group is not specified in o37."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "preserved_ids": ["n02", "n03", "n07", "n16", "l06"],
  "information_requests": [
    "Clarify the treatment temperature and heating mode for the high-temperature-treated uncoated group reported in o34.",
    "Clarify the heating mode used for the HD 700 °C tensile group reported in o37.",
    "Provide tensile specimen counts and variability or other uncertainty information for the reported groups, if available."
