      "availability": "relevant_visible",
      "assessment": "The LD coating's NiO diffraction peaks are reported to vanish at 700 °C, but that observation alone does not establish complete reduction of all NiO. A plausible alternative is that some NiO remains in fragmented, nanoscale, or poorly ordered domains whose diffraction is too weak or broad to resolve by laboratory XRD. This possibility is supported by reported residual nanoscale NiO after LH to 700 °C and by XPS reporting that NiO is only partly reduced and partly retained at 700 °C.",
      "scope": "The XRD observation is for LD coatings at 700 °C. The interfacial HRTEM observation is for imaged LD regions after LH to 700 °C; the XPS observation is surface-sensitive and reports LD results for both IH and LH at 700 °C.",
      "limitations": [
        "The HRTEM evidence concerns selected imaged regions after LH to 700 °C, so it does not establish the bulk amount of residual NiO or its state after IH.",
        "The reported XPS chemical-state result is surface-sensitive, and fitted component fractions were not inspected; it does not quantify bulk residual NiO.",
        "The packet does not provide XRD detection limits, quantitative phase fractions, or enough detail to confirm that the XRD and complementary measurements used samples with matched heating modes and histories."
      ],
      "rationale": "Peak disappearance establishes that NiO peaks were not detected in the reported laboratory XRD measurement, not that all NiO was converted. The residual nanoscale NiO reported by HRTEM and partial retention reported by XPS make loss of coherent diffraction from fragmented or poorly ordered NiO a candidate explanation, while leaving its amount and status in the XRD sample unresolved."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "candidate_alternative_interpretation",
      "target_ids": [
        "n14"
      ],
      "description": "The LD 700 °C XRD NiO peak disappearance may reflect fragmentation or disordering of residual NiO into nanoscale or low-abundance domains whose coherent diffraction falls below laboratory-XRD detectability, rather than complete conversion of all NiO to metallic Ni.",
      "basis_ids": [
        "o11",
        "o16",
        "o19"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "proposed_updates": [
    {
