      "availability": "relevant_visible",
      "assessment": "The reported optical modulation at 550 nm falls from 64% for NWT2 (150 °C) to 48% and 45% for NWT3 and NWT4. The higher-temperature films are also thicker (0.97 and 1.05 μm versus 0.90 μm for NWT2), and the text reports lower transmittance in both colored and bleached states above 150 °C. This makes greater optical path length a plausible alternative contributor to the smaller absolute transmittance difference, but does not establish it as the cause.",
      "scope": "Four films from one target and one deposition time, one reported thickness per film, and optical modulation at 550 nm; the state-transmittance comparison is qualitative in the supplied text.",
      "limitations": [
        "Replicate films and measurement uncertainty are not reported.",
        "The packet does not give numerical colored- and bleached-state transmittances for each film.",
