      "availability": "relevant_visible",
      "assessment": "The visible records support microglial changes in TAC retinas and responses to conditioned medium from endothelial cells exposed to TAC plasma. They do not uniquely establish that endothelial senescence-associated secretory factors, rather than residual TGFβ2 or another carried-over plasma-derived signal acting directly on microglia, cause those responses.",
      "scope": "Retinal microglial morphology and same-animal association with endothelial SA-β-gal in TAC versus Sham mice; phagocytosis and cytokine transcripts in neonatal primary mouse microglia given conditioned medium from plasma-exposed cultured endothelial cells.",
      "limitations": [
        "The in vivo morphology and correlation measurements are associations and do not identify the signal activating microglia.",
        "The conditioned-medium comparisons do not, in the visible records, establish that TGFβ2 was absent from the medium applied to microglia.",
        "The anti-TGFβ2 antibody reduced microglial readouts, but its precise timing for the phagocytosis comparison is unclear; antibody or TGFβ2 carryover is not ruled out.",
        "No visible observation directly compares endothelial secretome effects after selectively removing TGFβ2 from collected conditioned medium with direct TGFβ2 exposure of microglia."
      ],
      "rationale": "TAC retinas had altered Iba1+ microglial morphology and these metrics correlated with endothelial SA-β-gal (o36, o37). Conditioned medium from TAC-plasma-exposed endothelial cells increased microglial synaptosome fluorescence and cytokine transcripts relative to Sham-plasma conditioned medium (o38, o40), while anti-TGFβ2 treatment was associated with reduced readouts (o39, o40). These observations support a transferable signal but do not distinguish endothelial secreted factors from TGFβ2 or another factor carried into the transferred medium. The possibility is not demonstrated, and the medium-change protocol may reduce carryover, but carryover was not directly excluded in the visible records."
