      "scope": "Patient-level results among 411 patients with confirmed superficial LNTB at Xi'an Chest Hospital; retrospective observational comparisons using the PCR-fluorescent probe result as the endpoint.",
      "limitations": [
        "The comparison is observational and may be affected by selection or residual confounding.",
        "The reported adjusted model includes number of samples, but the supplied results do not report adjustment or stratification by specimen composition.",
        "These results do not establish an effect in other extrapulmonary TB populations."
      ],
      "rationale": "Surgery remained associated with positivity in the reported multivariate model, which included number of samples. However, neither the adjusted odds ratio nor the unadjusted cross-tabulation identifies a causal effect of surgery. The packet describes purulent and granulation-tissue specimens and different combinations of double samples, but supplies no comparison of positivity by specimen composition across surgical and non-surgical patients."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "reported_association",
