      "assessment": "The visible evidence does not support describing the 1700-hour result as excellent operational stability under ambient operation. It reports ambient storage without encapsulation: after 1700 h, the control retained 54% of its initial PCE, while SiC and SiC-APTES devices retained more than 90%. A separate operational measurement found stable photocurrent during a 150 s, 1-sun fixed-bias hold for all three device types. That short hold is not evidence of long-term operational stability under ambient conditions.",
      "scope": "The claim concerns p-i-n C-PSCs with the tested carbon pastes. The maximum reverse-scan PCE and the distinct 150 s illumination hold and 1700 h storage comparison are assessed only at their reported conditions.",
      "limitations": [
        "The ambient 1700 h result is a storage test, not a prolonged illuminated operational-stability test.",
        "The operational photocurrent observation covers only 150 s at fixed biases; it does not establish long-term operational stability.",
        "The visible storage result gives SiC and SiC-APTES retention as greater than 90%, without exact values or stated device counts in the main-text summary."
      ],
      "rationale": "The wording conflates ambient storage with operation. The evidence supports reporting ambient-storage PCE retention and a separate short operational photocurrent hold, but not the broader phrase “excellent operational stability under ambient operation.” The maximum-PCE component is separately supported by the champion reverse-scan result."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
